  "notes": "Refers to moral or behavioral decline, often with a strong negative connotation. The kanji {堕|だ} means \"to fall\" (as in {堕|お}ちる) and {落|らく} also means \"to fall,\" reinforcing the image of a downward slide.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {堕落|だらく}する: to become corrupt, to degenerate\n- {堕落|だらく}した{生活|せいかつ}: a dissolute lifestyle\n- {道徳|どうとく}の{堕落|だらく}: moral decline\n- {堕落|だらく}の{道|みち}: the path of corruption\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {腐敗|ふはい}: corruption — often used for institutional or political corruption\n- {退廃|たいはい}: decadence — focuses on cultural or artistic decline\n- {頽廃|たいはい}: same as above, with an older kanji variant\n\n{堕落|だらく} emphasizes personal moral decline, while {腐敗|ふはい} is more commonly used for systemic corruption.",
